Owner ruling, 2026-11-07 (card "Rule 13": add it to cat-harness#1116), on
the merge manager's proposal from that day's evidence: twice a lower
layer's main broke every downstream re-pin (check:test-gherkin and
translation:page-qa:check unrun downstream, the latter with a flag
mismatch; tree-walking checks without the declared build outputs skipped,
cat-harness-tools#1610 and #1616).

- prepare-merge §"A new gate in a lower layer must pass downstream": in
  the PR that adds the gate, it passes on its own main, says how
  downstream layers run it (shared reusable workflow, or opt-in with an
  exemption row), and shows a downstream dry run over a fresh
  folio-assistant mount.
- continual-progress: the same, in short.
- remote-mount §"Re-pinning": a re-pin moves pins only; a failure on a
  gate a lower layer just added is fixed in that layer.

